Implement user story SKY-006: Code review: Skyscanner mini-app

## Story Description
Review the full Skyscanner mini-app implementation across all src/ files. Checks: TypeScript strict compliance, test coverage (client, CLI, and server each have at least one test file), security (API key never logged or returned in responses, all query params validated), error handling completeness (non-200 upstream responses propagated correctly, missing-param responses return 400), and Express static-file safety (no path traversal). Produce a review document at /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md with findings organized by category. The review passes when all gating checks exit clean.

## Acceptance Criteria
- review/SKY-006-review.md is written to /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/ and contains sections for: TypeScript, Tests, Security, Error Handling, and Express Safety
- `tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with the project's tsconfig.json (strict mode enabled)
- `vitest run` exits 0 with no skipped or todo tests counted as passing
- Test files exist for each of the three layers: Skyscanner API client, CLI entry point, and Express server
- API key is not present in any log statement, console output, or HTTP response body in src/ files
- Every Express route that accepts query parameters returns HTTP 400 with a descriptive message when required params are missing or malformed
- Non-2xx responses from the upstream Skyscanner API are caught and forwarded to the caller as a structured error (not an unhandled exception)
- Static file serving uses a safe path resolution strategy — no user-supplied path segments are concatenated directly to __dirname or equivalent
- review/SKY-006-review.md includes a final PASS/FAIL verdict and, if FAIL, a prioritised list of blocking findings

